[21.208582, "o", "   - The filter should be a single string containing the complete jq filter expression\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[21.208595, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.208823, "o", "**Note on examples below**: In the following Data Schema sections, all content following the '\"'\"'#'\"'\"' symbol is just explanatory commentary and will NOT appear in the actual JSON files. These comments are only provided to clarify the structure and requirements.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[21.208869, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.208898, "o", "**Input Data Schema**:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.208959, "o", "The input JSON file '\"'\"'/app/users.json'\"'\"' is an array of user objects with the following structure:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> [\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[21.208984, "o", "\u001b[?2004h>   {\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.209049, "o", "    \"id\": 1,                  # Unique numeric identifier for the user\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[21.209079, "o", "> "]
[21.20912, "o", "    \"username\": \"john_doe\",   # User'\"'\"'s unique username (string)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.20919, "o", "    \"email\": \"john@example.com\",  # User'\"'\"'s email address (string)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[21.209216, "o", "> "]
[21.209269, "o", "    \"status\": \"active\",       # User status: '\"'\"'active'\"'\"' or '\"'\"'inactive'\"'\"'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[21.209293, "o", "> "]
[21.209363, "o", "    \"last_login\": \"2024-10-02T20:59:10.109812Z\",  # ISO 8601 timestamp (UTC) of the last login\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.209446, "o", "    \"roles\": [\"admin\", \"editor\"]  # Array of roles assigned to the user (may be empty)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.20947, "o", "  },\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   ...\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[21.209494, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> ]\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[21.209518, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.209542, "o", "**Output Data Schema**:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.209636, "o", "The output JSON file '\"'\"'/app/active_users_report.json'\"'\"' must be an array of objects with the following structure:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[21.209664, "o", "> [\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   {\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[21.209687, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.209736, "o", "    \"user_id\": 1,                 # Derived from '\"'\"'id'\"'\"' in input \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[21.209758, "o", "> "]
[21.209796, "o", "    \"username\": \"john_doe\",       # Retained from input \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[21.209838, "o", "> "]
[21.209863, "o", "    \"email\": \"john@example.com\",  # Retained from input \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[21.209872, "o", "> "]
[21.209932, "o", "    \"last_login\": \"2024-10-02\",   # Formatted from '\"'\"'last_login'\"'\"' in input\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[21.209951, "o", "> "]
[21.210002, "o", "    \"role_count\": 2,              # Count of '\"'\"'roles'\"'\"' from input\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[21.210026, "o", "> "]
[21.210103, "o", "    \"primary_role\": \"admin\"       # If '\"'\"'roles'\"'\"' is empty, this must be null (JSON null, not \"null\")\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[21.210127, "o", ">   },\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.21016, "o", "  ...\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ]\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[21.210186, "o", "> "]
[21.210212, "o", "**Requirements**:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[21.210303, "o", "- You must use jq to perform this transformation. Using other programming languages (e.g., Python, Ruby) is strictly prohibited.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
